WEBVTT

01:41.101 --> 01:44.020
SHINSHINKAI HEADQUARTERS
THE WAY OF KARATE

02:12.924 --> 02:16.094
That's why nobody wants to be around you.

02:16.177 --> 02:18.847
Not me, not Baki, not even your father.

02:22.308 --> 02:23.810
<i>He's exactly right.</i>

02:24.310 --> 02:26.980
<i>It's just like Yujiro Hanma said.</i>

02:27.063 --> 02:28.731
<i>Everyone senses it.</i>

02:29.482 --> 02:31.651
<i>On a whim, my father, Doppo Orochi,</i>

02:31.734 --> 02:34.487
<i>made me chairman of this place...</i>

02:35.697 --> 02:36.990
<i>but I don't have the smarts.</i>

02:37.907 --> 02:40.326
<i>Shinshinkai is the largest karate school,</i>

02:40.410 --> 02:42.495
<i>but I don't have the abilities
to be chairman.</i>

02:43.163 --> 02:46.291
<i>I don't have the history,
legends and charisma</i>

02:46.374 --> 02:48.001
<i>of my father, Doppo Orochi.</i>

02:50.086 --> 02:51.254
<i>I'll fight...</i>

02:52.172 --> 02:53.006
<i>I'll fight him.</i>

02:53.840 --> 02:55.717
INCOMING CALL

02:55.842 --> 02:58.261
Sir. No doubt about it.

02:58.344 --> 03:01.389
Both in appearance and size,
it was Pickle.

03:01.472 --> 03:03.349
No, he escaped.

03:05.685 --> 03:08.479
Talk about a godsend.

03:08.563 --> 03:10.273
I can't believe my good luck.

03:10.356 --> 03:11.441
SHINSHINKAI HEADQUARTERS

03:11.524 --> 03:13.276
There's no need to explain this to you.

03:14.152 --> 03:16.863
Shinshinkai isn't a bunch of hobbyists.

03:16.946 --> 03:19.782
Karate's Shinshinkai is
an organization of strength.

03:19.866 --> 03:24.662
Sea King Retsu was one of our teachers,
and we will avenge him.

03:25.371 --> 03:26.789
It's quite simple.

03:28.750 --> 03:30.752
Pickle is currently on the loose.

03:30.835 --> 03:32.921
The police are searching for him.

03:33.880 --> 03:36.507
There are 43,000 police officers,

03:36.591 --> 03:39.552
while there are 55,000 members
of Shinshinkai in Tokyo.

03:39.636 --> 03:42.555
We'll get a jump on them.

03:43.139 --> 03:46.559
Notify the chiefs
of the 220 branches in Tokyo.

03:47.310 --> 03:49.604
Leave no stone unturned in your search.

03:49.687 --> 03:50.563
That is all!

03:50.647 --> 03:52.482
Yes, sir!

03:53.399 --> 03:56.486
<i>We fight if we can win. Not if we can't.</i>

03:56.569 --> 03:58.821
<i>But this time,
winning or losing isn't a factor.</i>

03:58.905 --> 04:01.032
<i>Now is the time for action.</i>

04:01.115 --> 04:03.076
<i>There's no other way for us to show it.</i>

04:03.660 --> 04:06.037
<i>There's a million members in Shinshinkai.</i>

04:06.120 --> 04:09.582
<i>As a leader, I must feel the weight
of that number on my back!</i>

04:10.375 --> 04:12.585
That's a nice physique, mister.

04:12.669 --> 04:16.589
But I bet you've got a lot pent up,
if you know what I mean.

04:18.675 --> 04:21.552
All right, done. Just 3,000 yen.

04:21.636 --> 04:24.097
Nothing more and nothing less.

04:24.764 --> 04:27.100
Okay, one customer coming in!

04:28.268 --> 04:29.102
Huh?

04:29.185 --> 04:31.187
Sorry, pal.

04:31.271 --> 04:35.608
But this guy's with me.
Why don't you just leave him to me?

04:37.944 --> 04:41.364
I can tell he's not your friend.
You in the same business?

04:41.447 --> 04:43.866
No, it's not like that.

04:44.450 --> 04:45.618
What gang you with?

04:46.202 --> 04:50.373
I'm not in a gang or anything like that.
Just leave him to me.

04:50.456 --> 04:51.874
You a cop?

04:52.458 --> 04:53.626
No, not that either.

04:54.711 --> 04:57.380
You tryin' to pull some shit here? Huh?

05:04.887 --> 05:05.888
Well, well.

05:05.972 --> 05:08.224
Practice is over in the dojo.

05:08.308 --> 05:10.643
Who are you sitting and waiting for?

05:13.855 --> 05:15.148
Why don't you answer me?

05:16.274 --> 05:20.236
Don't tell me
you're trying to stop me, Dad.

05:20.737 --> 05:25.658
Katsumi, what is the most important thing
for a martial artist?

05:27.368 --> 05:29.203
It is to survive.

05:30.246 --> 05:33.416
Only ever fight someone
you know you can defeat.

05:34.125 --> 05:36.169
You can't win against him!

05:40.298 --> 05:42.383
When you were chairman,

05:42.467 --> 05:46.179
there'd be differences of opinion
at the branch chiefs' meetings at times.

05:46.262 --> 05:49.432
When that happened,
this is what you always said.

05:50.099 --> 05:52.643
"We're all karate fighters here."

05:52.727 --> 05:55.688
"Settle this with a match!"

05:56.981 --> 05:59.692
Sorry for making you say it first.

06:03.529 --> 06:06.699
Is it clear now what our intentions are?

06:07.283 --> 06:09.243
We're not here just for fun either.

06:09.827 --> 06:10.953
So leave him to us.

06:11.579 --> 06:13.289
It's just a single customer.

06:13.831 --> 06:16.709
If you're going to insist,
then go ahead. He's all yours.

06:16.793 --> 06:18.086
I owe you one.

06:18.586 --> 06:20.588
Next time, we'll come as customers.

06:21.214 --> 06:22.465
Yes, sir!

06:23.508 --> 06:25.468
Okay, Pickle, let's be going.

06:28.262 --> 06:29.097
Hey there.

06:31.682 --> 06:34.352
Hanayama...

06:35.186 --> 06:36.604
Good evening, sir!

06:39.690 --> 06:41.067
He's tough, huh?

06:42.652 --> 06:45.822
Hanayama, I'm Terada from Shinshinkai.

06:46.447 --> 06:48.282
Please listen to what I have to say.

06:48.366 --> 06:51.369
If we've offended you in some way,
I apologize.

06:52.703 --> 06:54.622
No need to apologize.

06:54.705 --> 06:57.375
Why don't you people just buzz off?

06:58.709 --> 07:01.879
That's pretty scary,
pointing a knife at me like that.

07:02.463 --> 07:04.132
But I hope you understand.

07:04.215 --> 07:07.385
This is the wish of Chairman Katsumi.

07:19.772 --> 07:20.898
<i>It was very puzzling.</i>

07:20.982 --> 07:22.191
Whoa!

07:22.275 --> 07:24.902
He's gripping the dagger blade!

07:24.986 --> 07:27.405
<i>He squeezed with incredible power.</i>

07:27.488 --> 07:29.907
You'll get cut, Boss!

07:29.991 --> 07:32.785
<i>The action he took
was essentially an attack.</i>

07:32.869 --> 07:37.165
<i>But it's clear that this man loves me.</i>

07:45.256 --> 07:46.674
Huh?

07:46.757 --> 07:48.009
Forgive me!

07:56.017 --> 07:59.979
Nobody would ever use that move
in a normal match.

08:00.521 --> 08:03.441
Especially not with their own father.

08:04.066 --> 08:06.444
But I'm sorry, Dad.

08:16.037 --> 08:17.955
You bastard!

08:31.010 --> 08:32.220
He's getting away!

08:34.805 --> 08:37.975
Please. Stay just a little longer.

08:56.202 --> 08:57.620
You're not going anywhere.

09:00.748 --> 09:01.624
Here we go!

09:08.214 --> 09:10.216
<i>It was the 21st century.</i>

09:10.299 --> 09:12.385
<i>The location was Tokyo, Japan,</i>

09:13.219 --> 09:15.888
<i>in a party district
filled with colorful neon signs.</i>

09:16.806 --> 09:20.643
<i>But even so,
the ancient warrior's mind saw</i>

09:20.726 --> 09:23.396
<i>something completely different
through his retinas.</i>

09:27.483 --> 09:30.403
<i>This man who stood in his way.</i>

09:30.987 --> 09:33.406
<i>This man who was smaller than him.</i>

09:34.407 --> 09:35.658
<i>He has the same strength</i>

09:35.741 --> 09:40.871
<i>as the worthy rivals
he once battled in his land.</i>

09:41.747 --> 09:45.668
<i>This guy was no bigger
than those little ones.</i>

09:46.586 --> 09:48.671
<i>Yet when it came to strength...</i>

09:51.007 --> 09:54.427
There's been some commotion
about a primitive man and dinosaurs,

09:55.094 --> 09:58.431
but that stuff doesn't work here.

10:02.518 --> 10:04.186
<i>It was no wonder.</i>

10:05.187 --> 10:08.441
<i>For this man was tied
to numerous social circumstances.</i>

10:08.524 --> 10:11.694
<i>Duty. Kindness. Obligation. Promises.</i>

10:13.112 --> 10:17.033
<i>From the logic and wisdom that sprung
from his network of relationships,</i>

10:17.116 --> 10:20.411
<i>he's gained a god-like strength
that defied human understanding.</i>

10:21.287 --> 10:26.083
<i>Pickle's rivals were nothing compared to
this man's god-like inner strength.</i>

10:27.293 --> 10:28.210
They stopped!

10:28.294 --> 10:29.253
Amazing!

10:29.337 --> 10:30.463
They're evenly matched!

10:31.172 --> 10:35.635
<i>He had been waiting to meet someone
worthy of fighting with all his strength.</i>

10:38.054 --> 10:39.221
It's over.

10:40.014 --> 10:41.724
I'm sorry for stopping you.

10:43.309 --> 10:46.312
You're late, Baki.

10:47.313 --> 10:50.232
Thanks for letting me know, Hanayama.

10:50.316 --> 10:52.318
Whoa! It's Baki Hanma!

10:52.401 --> 10:53.986
- Is it really him?
- He's here.

10:57.865 --> 11:00.201
Dang... Beautiful.

11:00.743 --> 11:02.828
I knew it. Just exquisite.

11:04.121 --> 11:05.289
- What?
-"Beautiful"?

11:05.373 --> 11:06.499
"Exquisite"?

11:07.875 --> 11:10.753
<i>Anything honed for one purpose alone,</i>

11:11.462 --> 11:14.590
<i>stripped of everything superfluous,
is beautiful.</i>

11:15.466 --> 11:17.677
<i>Whether the purpose is good or evil,</i>

11:17.760 --> 11:20.262
<i>the human heart can't help
but be enamored.</i>

11:20.930 --> 11:23.766
<i>The functional beauty
for running, leaping,</i>

11:23.849 --> 11:25.768
<i>catching and hunting.</i>

11:26.519 --> 11:30.022
<i>A body perfectly adapted solely
for the purpose of fighting.</i>

11:30.815 --> 11:34.652
<i>To Baki's eyes,
nothing seemed more beautiful.</i>

11:36.946 --> 11:38.072
<i>Would he kick?</i>

11:38.155 --> 11:40.658
<i>Would he punch? Would he strangle?</i>

11:41.659 --> 11:45.579
<i>He had mastered legendary martial arts
we've all heard of many times before.</i>

11:45.663 --> 11:48.999
<i>Baki Hanma was viewed
as the world's most powerful young man,</i>

11:49.083 --> 11:50.960
<i>so just how would he react?</i>

11:51.752 --> 11:53.379
<i>The group of fighters,</i>

11:53.462 --> 11:58.092
<i>the members of karate's Shinshinkai,
watched with bated breath.</i>

11:58.759 --> 12:02.722
Sorry. I wasn't planning on
doing anything when we met.

12:03.305 --> 12:07.017
When I heard from Tokugawa
that you had escaped,

12:07.768 --> 12:09.687
I asked Hanayama

12:10.354 --> 12:14.191
to let me know
if he caught wind of anything.

12:14.942 --> 12:17.570
I just wanted to meet you.

12:18.154 --> 12:21.949
I wanted to meet you really badly.
I really did.

12:22.616 --> 12:25.703
That's all. I'm sorry.

12:31.375 --> 12:32.209
Like this?

12:38.174 --> 12:41.969
<i>Having seen this body filled
with overpowering functional beauty...</i>

12:42.052 --> 12:44.555
<i>he knew it had also attained full mastery</i>

12:44.638 --> 12:48.476
<i>of the modern martial art of aikido.</i>

12:50.770 --> 12:53.272
<i>As if faced with coquetry
from a woman he adored,</i>

12:53.355 --> 12:56.901
<i>the boy was barely able
to maintain his self-control.</i>

12:56.984 --> 13:00.446
<i>Then the Hanma blood flowing in his veins</i>

13:01.071 --> 13:03.491
<i>suddenly burst its limits.</i>

13:09.079 --> 13:10.623
I... I'm sorry.

13:13.459 --> 13:14.293
I'm so sorry!

13:20.466 --> 13:22.510
You want me to go with you?

13:24.345 --> 13:25.179
And?

13:25.721 --> 13:28.140
Uh, he left.

13:28.224 --> 13:31.143
Baki and Hanayama went with him.

13:32.645 --> 13:34.355
Oh, really?

13:35.648 --> 13:37.149
I see.

13:37.233 --> 13:40.152
I'm sorry. We couldn't stop them.

13:40.736 --> 13:44.824
After knocking out my father,
I came here in high spirits,

13:45.324 --> 13:46.617
just to find that he's gone.

13:46.700 --> 13:47.910
That he left.

13:48.494 --> 13:51.664
So, the beloved girl
left her boorish boyfriend behind

13:52.289 --> 13:55.417
and went off
with her clever classmate, huh?

13:55.501 --> 13:57.169
I'm very sorry!

13:58.671 --> 14:00.422
But it's a good thing, right?

14:02.258 --> 14:04.134
Think about it.

14:04.218 --> 14:07.429
The original plan was
to get revenge for Master Retsu.

14:08.180 --> 14:11.392
I don't have to be the one
who accomplishes our goal.

14:12.059 --> 14:15.187
I'm fine if Baki Hanma
or Kaoru Hanayama does.

14:15.688 --> 14:19.567
We all feel the same
about the defeat of Master Retsu.

14:20.484 --> 14:22.528
It's fine if it isn't me.

14:23.028 --> 14:26.115
That's very generous, but are you sure?

14:26.740 --> 14:30.452
Shinshinkai came out in force
to avenge Master Retsu.

14:31.036 --> 14:33.789
What's more,
Terada was defeated by Pickle.

14:34.582 --> 14:37.710
Are you sure you want
someone else to handle Pickle?

14:37.793 --> 14:40.504
We have more than enough reason
to get him.

14:41.005 --> 14:43.215
Rather than Baki or Hanayama,

14:43.299 --> 14:46.760
shouldn't it be you, Master Katsumi,
who gets revenge?!

14:48.846 --> 14:52.474
Oh, I'm sorry, sir. I've gone too far.

14:52.558 --> 14:53.809
No, it's okay.

14:54.351 --> 14:56.812
By the way, Sakimura.
I've got a question for you.

14:56.896 --> 14:57.730
Yes, sir?

14:57.813 --> 15:01.233
Do you think I can defeat that Pickle?

15:02.818 --> 15:05.195
I can't be sure if it's true,

15:05.279 --> 15:07.489
but they say
he's a natural enemy to <i>the</i> T-Rex,

15:07.573 --> 15:09.491
and the most powerful warrior in history.

15:09.575 --> 15:12.995
Do you really think that I,
Katsumi Orochi,

15:13.078 --> 15:15.998
the hopeless, spoiled son
of a great master,

15:16.582 --> 15:19.752
can defeat this monster?!

15:26.216 --> 15:27.051
Sorry.

15:28.010 --> 15:30.971
We fight if we can win.
We don't fight if we can't.

15:31.055 --> 15:34.266
But I'm the one who said winning
or losing wasn't a factor this time.

15:39.605 --> 15:41.523
Everyone, I'm begging you.

15:41.607 --> 15:45.027
For Master Retsu, for Shinshinkai,

15:46.028 --> 15:48.280
please help me out!

15:48.364 --> 15:51.033
Yes, sir!

15:53.744 --> 15:55.537
He just might change.

16:04.880 --> 16:06.548
You damn fool!

16:06.632 --> 16:08.550
Where the heck did you wander off to?!

16:08.634 --> 16:12.054
Dang, I never thought he'd come here.

16:12.680 --> 16:17.309
So, what is it you want to do
now that you've brought me here?

16:17.893 --> 16:21.814
Baki, isn't it obvious
what you're gonna do here?

16:21.897 --> 16:24.566
You know what's done here, don't you?

16:24.650 --> 16:28.570
He's picking a fight with you, Baki!

16:29.321 --> 16:30.322
That's what I thought.

16:31.156 --> 16:33.325
You are picking a fight, aren't you?

16:33.409 --> 16:35.077
Then I'll have to accept.

16:35.160 --> 16:39.164
Are you sure you want to get
this naive guy involved?

16:41.667 --> 16:42.584
Huh?

16:42.668 --> 16:45.462
No, I guess it's none of my business.

16:46.130 --> 16:48.590
It seems he wants to fight as well.

16:48.674 --> 16:50.676
You saved me, Hanayama.

16:51.176 --> 16:55.180
I was about to repeat the same mistake
I made five years ago.

16:55.681 --> 17:01.103
I entered the territory
of innocent people living in peace,

17:02.271 --> 17:04.982
<i>and dragged them into a fight
for their lives.</i>

17:06.692 --> 17:08.360
I caused nothing but trouble.

17:08.444 --> 17:09.862
Oh, dear me.

17:09.945 --> 17:12.614
I was just getting a little bored.

17:13.323 --> 17:15.701
I just wanted to have a little fun.

17:16.702 --> 17:19.621
But I let those feelings
get the better of me.

17:21.206 --> 17:23.167
I was about to do something stupid.

17:44.021 --> 17:46.023
He's dancing! Whoa!

17:50.235 --> 17:52.404
He's raising his fist above his head.

17:53.113 --> 17:54.156
It's the same.

17:54.740 --> 17:58.160
<i>In the past as in the present,
victory is celebrated the same way.</i>

17:59.828 --> 18:01.747
It only took a single blow.

18:01.830 --> 18:04.958
Maybe we should take him away
before he's eaten.

18:12.549 --> 18:13.550
One lap.

18:14.134 --> 18:17.304
Go one lap around the dojo using these.

18:18.138 --> 18:21.892
Then use that grip
to harden your fists and punch!

18:24.895 --> 18:27.648
Naturally, one blow
would knock out a human.

18:27.731 --> 18:30.818
And if you do it right, even a bull.

18:39.827 --> 18:40.953
<i>A bull, huh?</i>

18:42.663 --> 18:45.457
<i>It would be a lot easier
if I was just facing a bull.</i>

18:46.375 --> 18:48.210
<i>In any case, what'll I do?</i>

18:48.293 --> 18:52.214
<i>I'm a karate fighter,
so what else can I rely on besides karate?</i>

18:56.718 --> 18:57.845
Retsu!

18:57.928 --> 19:01.306
My friend, I have heard a strange rumor.

19:01.807 --> 19:05.978
In the match earlier, I suffered defeat.

19:06.687 --> 19:10.065
I heard that you members of Shinshinkai
are trying to get vengeance.

19:11.191 --> 19:12.985
I'm the one who demanded it.

19:13.068 --> 19:14.278
Incomprehensible!

19:14.945 --> 19:17.865
It's absurd to think that you,
who I have trained,

19:17.948 --> 19:21.243
could possibly obtain vengeance
on someone even I had no chance against.

19:21.326 --> 19:22.870
You're exactly right.

19:23.662 --> 19:27.082
We tried to avenge you,
our superior in the world of martial arts.

19:27.166 --> 19:28.750
It is pure insolence.

19:29.459 --> 19:30.752
But I want revenge.

19:30.836 --> 19:35.132
Now I know the truth that the skill
of the great fighter, Sea King Retsu,

19:35.215 --> 19:37.009
was no match for him.

19:37.718 --> 19:40.762
Even so, in fact, because of that fact,

19:41.513 --> 19:44.016
I want to face him with my karate!

19:45.767 --> 19:46.727
Just as I thought.

19:47.311 --> 19:51.064
You tell others you're avenging me,
because you're indebted to me.

19:51.148 --> 19:53.025
But here your true feelings come out.

19:53.108 --> 19:55.736
Vengeance is a slogan
we use for convenience.

19:56.278 --> 19:59.489
If someone is strong,
we want to fight them.

19:59.573 --> 20:00.532
That's how we are.

20:00.616 --> 20:03.535
Do you think your karate can defeat him?

20:03.619 --> 20:04.661
I don't know.

20:05.370 --> 20:09.166
If I've got a chance to win, I'll fight.
But I won't if I don't.

20:09.249 --> 20:11.793
I've decided this isn't
that kind of fight.

20:13.879 --> 20:16.048
You've changed, Katsumi.

20:17.966 --> 20:18.800
Thanks.

20:20.886 --> 20:24.681
As you can see, I've also changed in form,

20:25.224 --> 20:27.309
but I've got a lot I can teach you.

20:27.935 --> 20:28.769
Katsumi.

20:29.394 --> 20:33.523
There have been
4,000 great years of kung fu history.

20:33.607 --> 20:35.817
Would you like to carry on
its 4,001st year?

20:37.903 --> 20:38.862
SHAOLIN TEMPLE

20:38.946 --> 20:41.156
<i>If you go through the history of karate,</i>

20:41.240 --> 20:43.450
<i>you'll arrive at Mount Song in China.</i>

20:43.951 --> 20:47.579
<i>It eventually crossed
to the Ryukyu islands,</i>

20:47.663 --> 20:50.457
<i>and made unique progress,
shaped by the environment.</i>

20:50.540 --> 20:54.628
<i>In 1922, Gichin Funakoshi brought it
to mainland Japan,</i>

20:54.711 --> 20:56.338
<i>and it became what it is today.</i>

20:56.421 --> 20:59.341
Katsumi, karate is still young.

21:00.259 --> 21:03.011
It's only been 500 years
since its arrival in Okinawa.

21:03.095 --> 21:06.223
Today, as everyone
looks toward its 501st year,

21:06.306 --> 21:09.434
you are the only one
who is ready for the 4,001st year.

21:09.935 --> 21:13.355
Let me be the one to teach you the art.

21:14.481 --> 21:15.941
I appreciate your desire to.

21:16.942 --> 21:19.069
As young as it is,

21:19.152 --> 21:22.364
as underdeveloped as it is,
I want it to hit the 501st year as it is.

21:23.949 --> 21:26.368
I want to follow the way of karate.

21:26.952 --> 21:28.954
It can only be karate.

21:31.290 --> 21:34.084
I almost meddled where I shouldn't have.

21:34.167 --> 21:35.377
I'm sorry.

21:37.212 --> 21:38.714
Incidentally, Katsumi,

21:38.797 --> 21:42.384
could I assist you with that 501st year?

21:43.468 --> 21:44.469
Well...

21:44.970 --> 21:47.973
<i>No, I can't let him do that.</i>

21:48.056 --> 21:49.516
<i>If he gets involved,</i>

21:49.599 --> 21:53.645
<i>our 501st year and his 4,001st year
will get all tangled up.</i>

21:54.730 --> 21:57.899
Please, allow me to assist
with your 501st year.

21:58.900 --> 22:01.403
<i>Oh, well, I guess it's okay.</i>

22:02.321 --> 22:03.155
Gladly!

22:03.947 --> 22:07.075
<i>A union with the 4,001st year of kung fu.</i>

22:07.617 --> 22:11.413
<i>Yes, this was the 501st year of karate.</i>

22:11.496 --> 22:15.667
<i>A revolutionary trail
is about to be trodden.</i>

22:16.918 --> 22:20.047
That guy really has changed.
